  "notes": [
    "`comprehended` requires a LOOP_HEAD: a comprehension is an implicit loop with a filter, and rendering it as one flat expression hides a branch the owner can change.",
    "`guarded` requires FINALLY as its own block: the finally body runs on both the normal and the exceptional path, so folding it into either one loses an edge.",
    "`matched` has three outcomes; the wildcard case is an outcome, not an absence."
  ],
  "proves": "The CFG covers branches, for and while loops, try/except/finally, with, comprehensions, match and early exits. Each function below names the block kinds its shape forces, and the block kinds its shape rules out.",
